- OWNERSHIP SPLIT: The build host proves unsigned native macOS `build-for-testing` only and reports runtime as explicitly deferred to `TASK-260822-3q4grm`; that task owns signed fixture-host/XCUITest runtime proof on the dedicated test Mac. No provider/system extension is built by either UI-test scheme; no app/provider installation, native Mac fixture launch, VPN preference, tunnel, route, interface, packet-filter, or DNS operation runs here.
- VALIDATION ANOMALY: A post-rework full `swift test` run exited `1` because the unrelated libssh2 `clientAndServerRekey` M0 gate did not observe `.closed` before its assertion; the run otherwise reached all 455 tests and reported the existing 25 known ReluxNIOSSH issues. An immediate exact `mandatoryGate` rerun passed all 18 argument rows (exit `0`, nine known unavailable-adapter issues), so the failure is retained as a transport-suite timing anomaly rather than attributed to the UI-test infrastructure.
- REVIEW REWORK: POSIX `set -e` is suppressed inside a function used as an `if` condition, so the first smoke implementation could return a successful Xcode status after a failed screenshot extractor. The runtime row now captures extractor and validator exits explicitly, independently validates the schema/count and both non-empty step-named PNGs, and records separate Xcode, artifact, row, and aggregate exits. A production-script regression injects extractor exit `42` and proves the aggregate exits `1`; the real build-host smoke and all 455 Swift tests pass after the fix.

